{"name":"Up North","hex":"#6f9587","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"up north","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["In the northern part of an area, country etc.","In jail, in prison."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/up_north"}],"entries":[{"title":"Northern England","blocks":[{"text":"Northern England, or the North of England, often referred to as simply the North, is the northern part of England and mainly corresponds to the historic counties of Cheshire, Cumberland, Durham, Lancashire, Northumberland, Westmorland and Yorkshire. Officially, it is a grouping of three statistical regions: the North East, the North West, and Yorkshire and the Humber, which had a combined population of 15.5 million at the 2021 census, an area of 37,331 km2 and 18 cities."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Northern_England.svg/330px-Northern_England.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northern_England"},{"title":"Up North (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Up North is a 2018 Nigerian drama film produced by Anakle Films and Inkblot Productions, and directed by Tope Oshin. The screenplay was written by Naz Onuzo and Bunmi Ajakaiye, based on a story from Editi Effiong. It was mainly shot in Bauchi, with a one-week shoot in Lagos."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/30/Up_North_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Up_North_(film)"},{"title":"North","blocks":[{"text":"North is one of the four compass points or cardinal directions. It is the opposite of south and is perpendicular to east and west. North is a noun, adjective, or adverb indicating direction or geography."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Compass_Rose_English_North.svg/330px-Compass_Rose_English_North.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.o